<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of The Hague (1795)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1795">1795</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of The Hague was signed on 16 May 1795 between the French Republic and the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavian-republic">Batavian Republic</a>. It made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, ceded Dutch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maastricht">Maastricht</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venlo">Venlo</a>, required an indemnity of 100 million guilders and the upkeep of a French army of occupation. It bound the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> to France's wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-the-hague-1795.jpg" alt="Treaty of The Hague (1795)" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian Josi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Treaty_of_The_Hague_(1795).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
